# @ResponseMessage on Every HTTP Endpoint

Every HTTP route handler (`@Get`, `@Post`, `@Put`, `@Patch`, `@Delete`) **must** be decorated with `@ResponseMessage('…')` from `@ross2p/common`.

The `ResponseInterceptor` in `CommonModule` reads this metadata and includes a human-readable `message` field in the `SuccessResponse<T>` envelope.

## Rule

Add `@ResponseMessage('Descriptive message')` directly above every HTTP route handler decorator.

## Correct pattern

```typescript
import { ResponseMessage } from '@ross2p/common';

@Controller('session')
export class SessionController {
  @Post('sign-out')
  @ResponseMessage('Signed out successfully')
  async signOut(...) { ... }

  @Get()
  @ResponseMessage('Sessions retrieved')
  async listSessions(...) { ... }
}
```

## Incorrect pattern

```typescript
@Controller('session')
export class SessionController {
  @Post('sign-out')           // ← missing @ResponseMessage
  async signOut(...) { ... }
}
```

## Source

`@ResponseMessage` is defined in `libs/common/src/decorators/response-message.decorator.ts` and exported from `@ross2p/common`.
